# Minuet in G, the melody (repertoire plan: minuet-in-g-melody). The upper voice of the minuet in
# the 1725 Notebook for Anna Magdalena Bach (BWV Anh. 114, now credited to Christian Petzold): two
# halves of 16 bars, each played twice. Guitar sounds an octave below where it is written, so this
# part reads exactly like the keyboard right hand. First position (finger 1 on fret 1, finger 4 on
# fret 4) except bars 17 and 18: during the long G that ends the first half, slide the hand up so
# finger 1 sits at fret 5 (A on string 1), finger 3 at fret 7 (B) and finger 4 at fret 8 of
# string 2 (G); after the A that starts bar 18, come back to first position.
title: Minuet in G (melody)
id: minuet-in-g-melody
composer: Christian Petzold
source: Minuet in G from the Notebook for Anna Magdalena Bach (1725), BWV Anh. 114, long credited to J. S. Bach; upper voice, arranged for Sixstring Academy
arranger: Sixstring Academy
licence: Public domain (Petzold died in 1733); this arrangement is original to Sixstring Academy
difficulty: 3
tags: minuet, baroque, 3/4, repeats
tempo: 100
time: 3/4
key: G

track: Melody
role: lead
